# Paths that must NOT be synced to the PUBLIC repo
# (github.com/databricks-solutions/solution-builder).
#
# This repo (databricks-field-eng/industry-demo-prompts) is the PRIVATE source;
# the public repo is a mirror. Whatever job mirrors private→public MUST exclude
# every path listed here. Each is internal-only content (live Demo-West links,
# internal catalogs) that should never appear in the open-source project.
#
# Syntax: gitignore-style globs, repo-root-relative.

# Internal deploy overlays — real workspace/Lakebase IDs, endpoint names, admin
# emails for the official prod / staging / FEVM deployments. No secrets, but
# internal-only. The public repo ships only the *.example templates.
app/databricks.prod.yml
app/databricks.staging.yml
app/databricks.prod-fevm.yml
# The FEVM deploy TEMPLATE also names FEVM (internal) — strip it too. (Unlike
# the other *.yml.example files, which are public.)
app/databricks.prod-fevm.yml.example

# FEVM integration module — internal-only (Solution Builder / GTM AI Tooling
# team managed deployment). FEVM is not a public product; this is the
# workspace-discovery + provisioning skin on top of the generic remote-deploy
# core. The generic core (paste-URL scale tier) SHIPS to public; only this skin
# is stripped. Now a single self-contained package (mcp.py + routes.py +
# models.py + README.md); ../router.py imports it under try/except so removing
# this whole directory leaves the app booting cleanly. See backend/fevm/README.md.
app/src/demo_prompt_generator/backend/fevm/

# Internal FEVM redeploy runbook + any FEVM-specific ops scripts. The GENERIC
# per-region onboarding script (app/scripts/remote-deploy/) SHIPS to public;
# only this FEVM-named folder is stripped.
app/scripts/fevm/
